  "history": "Bessemer Venture Partners grew out of Bessemer Securities, the family office Henry Phipps founded in New York in 1911, and became an independent venture firm in 1981. The bets that made it were Staples, Ciena, VeriSign and Skype, followed by LinkedIn, Yelp, Shopify, Twilio, Pinterest, Toast and Anthropic. In September 2026 it raised $5.75 billion, $1.75 billion for early-stage companies and $4 billion for growth; the track record on this page leaves out its buyout arm, BVP Forge.",
